 its volume and poem number. The results were mostly tables of contents and index lists for other Man'yōshū poems, such as the Hitomaro collection poems in Books 11 and 12, so none of them matches the query.\n\nOne result does confirm that 《万葉集》や《出雲国風土記》に広く使われているカンナビ,カンナビヤマ(神奈備)がある, which supports the reading of 神奈備 as a sacred mountain. I can't confirm the poem's location from these results.\n\nTo pin down the number, I'd suggest searching the first line in kana (かんなびに ひもろきたてて いはへども) together with 万葉集 or 万葉歌, or checking a database such as 万葉集 at e-Text or the NIJL Man'yōshū database, which lists poems by their first lines."], "durationSeconds": 6.688842791999999, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01JYiMdSzAcQP9DLkBqB8Pj4", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
