oem. None of the results contain the phrases 「ひもろき立てて」 or 「人の心は守りあへぬもの」, so I can't confirm which Man'yōshū poem they come from or its wording.\n\nThe results only offered general background on the anthology. A Tottori prefecture document says it contains 4516首の和歌が全20巻に収められています, and a Nara prefecture document notes it has 約四五〇〇首の歌, with many poems naming living things.\n\nSuggested next steps:\n- The standard modern spelling is usually 「ひもろぎ」 (with ぎ), so 「ひもろぎ立てて」 may match better.\n- Searching the phrase 「守りあへぬ」 alone, or with 万葉集 and a volume number, may help.\n- A full-text Man'yōshū database, such as the NIJL 国文学研究資料館 database, would let you search the exact wording."], "durationSeconds": 5.912770833999999, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01M7bb3Sy3PsPqwB2vjb1xNb", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
